  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN259.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">uṭaṉpōkku nērnta tōḻi talaimakaṭ kuṭaṉpōkkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante, who had agreed to an elopement, spoke to HER about elopement.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN259.1">
        <l>vēlum viḷaṅkiṉa viḷaiyaru miyaṉṟaṉar</l>
        <l>tārun taiyiṉa taḻaiyun toṭuttaṉa</l>
        <l>nilanī raṟṟa vemmai nīṅkap</l>
        <l>peyaṉīr talaiiya vulavai yilainīttuk</l>
        <l>kuṟumuṟi <supplied>yī</supplied>ṉṟaṉa maraṉē naṟumalar</l>
        <l>vēyntaṉa pōlat  tōṉṟip palavuṭaṉ</l>
        <l>ṟēmpaṭap potuḷiṉa poḻilē kā<supplied>ṉa</supplied>mu</l>
        <l>naṉinaṉ ṟākiya paṉinīṅku vaḻināṭ</l>
        <l>pāleṉap parattaru nilaviṉ mālaip</l>
        <l>pōtuvan taṉṟu tūtē nīyuṅ</l>
        <l>kalaṅkā maṉattai yāki yeṉcoṉ</l>
        <l>ṉayantaṉai koṇmō neñcamar takuvi</l>
        <l>teṟṟi yulaṟiṉum vayalai vāṭiṉu</l>
        <l>nocci meṉciṉai vaṇarkural cāyiṉu</l>
        <l><supplied>ni</supplied>ṉṉiṉu maṭava ṇaṉi<supplied>niṉ</supplied> ṉayanta</l>
        <l>vaṉṉai yalla ṟāṅkiniṉ ṉaiyar</l>
        <l>pulimaruḷ cemma ṉōkki</l>
        <l>valiyā yiṉṉun tōykaniṉ mulaiyē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">The spears shine, the young men advance,</l>
        <l corresp="2">the garlands have been fixed, the foliage has been linked.</l>
        <l corresp="3">Since the heat left by [means of] which the water in the ground had ceased,</l>
        <l corresp="4">as the [old] leaves left the dry twigs on which rainwater had been showered</l>
        <l>the trees have brought forth short shoots. Appearing as if</l>
        <l>covered with fragrant blossoms the groves have become</l>
        <l>full [of them], many together, so that nectar falls. And on the last day</l>
        <l>when the dew leaves by which the forest has become very good</l>
        <l>the evening time, with moonlight that spreads like milk,</l>
        <l corresp="5-10">has come as a messenger. You too,</l>
        <l corresp="11">being of unperturbed mind, keenly</l>
        <l corresp="12">take in my word, oh befitting one who abides in [my] heart:</l>
        <l corresp="13">Even if the Teṟṟi were to wither, even if the purslane faded,</l>
        <l corresp="14">even if the curved [flower] clusters on the soft Nocci branches were to bow over,</l>
        <l corresp="15">bearing the unhappiness of mother</l>
        <l corresp="16">who much dotes on you, she who is more foolish than you,</l>
        <l corresp="17">looking at the tiger-like haughtiness of your men folk,</l>
        <l corresp="18">[my] strong one, let [me] touch your breast again.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

